 "_comment": "Moving parts: two sashes named Robe on the chest (named), an unnamed four-bone strap on the pelvis (hanging chain), back hair and a ribbon on a hat (named). The short pouch chain, the finger chain, a hairpin and a ring-shaped hair loop stay body bones. The two breast bones move only with breast motion on; renamed, they are still found as a mirrored pair in front of the chest. A DAZ-style lPectoral/rPectoral pair on the spine counts as breasts too. A pistol in the left hand (its bones are marked as gun bones at inspection) carries an unnamed three-link charm hanging below it and a strap, which move; its slide, magazine and a sideways fin stay on the gun. Named charms move anywhere: a key chain on the hand, a necklace pendant and a dangle earring (dangle wins over earring). An unnamed tag hanging from the hand stays a body bone. Butts are separate from breasts and move only with butt motion on: a named Butt_L/R pair on the pelvis and an unnamed mirrored pair low behind the hips. Each foot has a toe on the ground and a longer boot flap pointing backwards; only the lowest child (the toe) tells the facing direction, so the renamed breasts are still found in front. butt_names lists names that are and are not butts (尻尾 is a tail, Button is not a butt).",
